{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_circuit_breaker_circuitbreaker", "label": "CircuitBreaker", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Wickelt jede () => Promise<T>-Factory und kurzschliesst, wenn der Fehler anhaelt. Traegt Zustand ueber Calls hinweg - das unterscheidet ihn von Retry, der jeden Call unabhaengig behandelt.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_circuit_breaker_closed", "label": "Closed-Zustand", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Calls gehen durch, Fehler werden gezaehlt; ein Erfolg setzt den Zaehler auf 0 zurueck. Bei maxFailures aufeinanderfolgenden Fehlern uebergeht der Breaker zu Open.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_circuit_breaker_open", "label": "Open-Zustand", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Calls schlagen sofort fehl; kein Traffic erreicht den Downstream. Der Uebergang zu Half-open ist kein geplantes Aufwachen - der Breaker prueft lazy beim naechsten call(), ob Date.now() >= nextProbeAt.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_circuit_breaker_halfopen", "label": "Half-open-Zustand", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Der erste Call nach dem Reset-Timeout wird durchgelassen: Erfolg schliesst, Fehler oeffnet wieder mit frischem nextProbeAt. Der Breaker serialisiert nicht - parallele Calls gehen auch durch, die Uebergaenge werden vom ersten Vollenden getrieben.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_circuit_breaker_circuitbreakeropenerror", "label": "CircuitBreakerOpenError", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": null, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_circuit_breaker_circuitbreakertimeouterror", "label": "CircuitBreakerTimeoutError", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Ein Call, der callTimeoutMs ueberschreitet, rejected damit und zaehlt als Fehler. callTimeoutMs ganz weglassen deaktiviert den Per-Call-Timeout.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_circuit_breaker_isfailure", "label": "isFailure-Praedikat", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Gibt isFailure(err) false zurueck, umgeht der Fehler die Zaehlung - das Promise rejected weiterhin zum Aufrufer. Fuer Fehler, die kein Service-Fehler sind: 404s, Validierungsfehler.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_circuit_breaker_onstatechange", "label": "onStateChange", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Feuert bei jedem Uebergang, einschliesslich erzwungener via setState. Gedacht zum Verdrahten in Logging- oder Metriken-Pipelines; breaker.state liest den Zustand synchron.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_circuit_breaker_setstate", "label": "setState (manueller Override)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Meist fuer Tests und Admin-Endpoints. Zu setState aus regulaerem Produktionscode zu greifen bedeutet meist, dass der Breaker nicht richtig konfiguriert ist.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_circuit_breaker_retry_inside_breaker", "label": "Retry innerhalb eines Breaker-Calls", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Der Retry handhabt die Per-Call-Resilienz, der Breaker die 'hoer auf, die kaputte Dep zu haemmern'-Koordination. Den Retry ausserhalb des Breakers zu legen bedeutet, durch CircuitBreakerOpenErrors zu retrien - sinnlos.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_circuit_breaker_breaker_per_dependency", "label": "Ein Breaker pro logischer Abhaengigkeit", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Ein einzelner Breaker fuer zwei unverwandte Abhaengigkeiten loest bei einem von beiden Fehlern aus und sperrt beide aus. Ausserdem: einen Breaker als Actor-Feld zu halten setzt ihn bei jedem Restart zurueck - fuer restart-ueberlebenden Zustand in eine Extension oder einen Parent heben.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_circuit_breaker_closed", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_circuit_breaker_circuitbreaker", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_circuit_breaker_open", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_circuit_breaker_circuitbreaker", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_circuit_breaker_halfopen", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_circuit_breaker_circuitbreaker", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_circuit_breaker_open", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_circuit_breaker_circuitbreakeropenerror", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_circuit_breaker_circuitbreaker", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_circuit_breaker_circuitbreakertimeouterror", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_circuit_breaker_isfailure", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_circuit_breaker_closed", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_circuit_breaker_onstatechange", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_circuit_breaker_circuitbreaker", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "do